 ## Overview
-Voxel Ambient Occlusion estimates ambient occlusion for a surface point by sampling the solidity of surrounding voxels relative to the surface normal, simulating light blockage from adjacent geometry [S1, unofficial]. It operates in world space using voxel occupancy data, distinguishing it from screen-space techniques like Vicinity Occlusion Mapping [S3, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of voxel-based neighbor counting [17927-voxel-based-neighbor-counting.md].
